; t29_fncall.n — v16 dynamic calls: 'x on a variable holding a fn cell.
; The cell's declared arity takes the stack below — no list packing.
; (' executes any function: label, variable, method — no call/send words.)
; Run: nk comp/tests/t29_fncall.n

; 1. 'x on a var holding a named fn
addf f!
3 4 'f 7 eq check

; 2. 'x on a var holding an anonymous fn
: x! x 2 mul ret m!
[5] m apply 10 eq check
5 'm 10 eq check

; 4. wrong arity on a var-held fn dies at the site naming the label,
;    and try contains it
: 1 'f ret try ok# _#
ok 0 eq check

; 5. fn cells thread through calls without list churn
: x! x 1 add ret bump!
10 'bump 'bump 'bump 13 eq check

; 6. a named fn via 'name (label resolution) still works alongside
3 4 'addf 7 eq check

ret
addf: a! b!
  ret a b add
